  "published": "2025-09-17T02:53:22.153Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Effortlessly build and refactor pipelines with AutoPipe:\n      - Create processors by inheriting from AutoProcessor.\n      - Annotate methods with [Run] to execute them in the pipeline; rename methods freely without refactoring dependencies.\n      - Add new parameters by returning them from methods prefixed with Get, or return anonymous objects for multiple values.\n      - Use attributes to control pipeline behavior:\n        [Run] - Mark a method to be executed in the pipeline.\n        [RunAll] - Execute all methods in the processor.\n        [Skip] - Exclude a method from execution.\n        [Aka(\"Custom Name\")] - Alias methods and processors for flexible referencing.\n        [Is(\"Description\")] - Add descriptions for better debugging and documentation.\n        [Order(15)] - Specify execution order for processors and methods.\n        [After(\"Previous\")] - Define execution dependencies between processors.\n        [Or(\"Default value\")] - Provide fallback values for missing properties.\n        [Required(Message = \"Cannot proceed without this parameter\", Halt = true)] - Enforce required parameters and control pipeline flow.\n        [Strict] - Require all parameters for a method.\n\n      For more details, visit the documentation: https://github.com/wittylion/AutoPipe/wiki",
